blizzard casually announced a new  survival game ea is working on three new  star wars titles and more  blizzard has announced that it's working  on a new survival game that's set for pc  and consoles and it's gonna be in a  brand new universe unfortunately that's  about all we know at this point along  with a look at some concept art for the  project a surprise blizzard blog post  reads we are going on a journey to a  whole new universe home to a brand new  survival game for pc and console a place  full of heroes we have yet to meet  stories yet to be told and adventures  yet to be lived a vast realm of  possibility waiting to be explored the  announcement largely serves as a  recruitment ad for the project blizzard  is looking to fill a number of positions  for the game including level designer  lead software engineer senior character  artist and more this new survival game  will be blizzard's first new ips since  overwatch in 2016 and it's been reported  that even some of the most disgruntled  blizzard employees rave about this game  and the team that's working on it the  announcement of the survival game comes  in the wake of microsoft beginning the  process of acquiring activision blizzard  and a 69 billion dollar deal considering  activision blizzard is in the process of  becoming part of microsoft it's unclear  if this new game will come to  playstation or nintendo switch or if it  will be an xbox console exclusive  ea has announced major plans to create  some more star wars games with its  partners and studios developing three  new games in total including a sequel to  jedi fallen order there's also going to  be an fps and a strategy title respawn  is overseeing the development of all  three according to reporter jeff grubb  reespan's new star wars fps is being  made by the same team that developed the  vr game medal of honor above and beyond  however the new game is not a vr title  and is apparently a traditional fps  however ea did not announce any new star  wars battlefront games the series was  headed up by battlefield studio dice  which apparently pitched battlefront 3  but the licensing costs were reportedly  too high all of these titles will be  coming from respawn alongside continued  work on apex legends and another  unannounced new title but it's worth  remembering that ea no longer holds the  exclusive license for star wars games on  console and pc this is why we'll be  seeing a lot more star wars in the not  so distant future ubisoft is developing  its own new open world star wars game  while zynga is making a free to play  shooter called star wars hunters and we  can't forget that the knights of the old  republic remake is also in the works for  ps5 and pc from aspire media jedi fallen  order is a gorgeous game and i still  have friends that hop back into it to  this day are you looking forward to a  sequel let me know why or why not in the  comments  and if you've been keeping up with new  world then a huge patch is coming to  shake up the end game using mutated  expedition orbs which can be crafted or  purchased from faction vendors players  can attempt more challenging versions of  expeditions with different modifiers  each week with extra powerful rewards on  the line players will be scored on their  performance with number of kills wipes  and completion time all factoring into  the equation higher scores means access  to higher difficulties and better  rewards going hand in hand with  expedition mutators is the new umbral  shard upgrade system by gaining umbral  shards from mutated expeditions players  can raise the max gear score of their  equipment up to 6.25 but while in-game  is the focus of the latest new world  update there's plenty of smaller changes  that should go a long way towards  improving the game as well the good news  for players who are still working their  way towards max level the speed at which  players gain levels from levels 25 to 45  is being increased by 20  amazon states that 